<title>SINGAPORE: India tenders to sell July 2-4 Bombay naphtha.</title>
<headline>India tenders to sell July 2-4 Bombay naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has issued a tender to sell 25,000 tonnes of high aromatic naphtha (HAN) lifting July 2-4 from Bombay on the west coast, industry sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The tender closes on June 19 and is valid for a day.</p>
<p>IOC's last HAN cargo from Bombay, lifting June 5-7, was sold through tender to a Dutch trader at $41 per tonne below Japanese sppot naphtha quotes, on a free-on-board basis.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
</text>
